# Motion capture harness — generated, never committed. The bundle is rebuilt by
# `npm run motion:capture` and the frames are the run's output, not source.
tests/motion/bundle.js
tests/motion/bundle.css
tests/motion/frames/

# Screenshots are a run's OUTPUT, not source. The launch smoke writes a numbered
# set to scratchpad/launch-smoke/ on every run, browser guards drop stills
# beside their scratch scripts, and none of it is worth a diff — it is a
# megabyte of PNG that changes on every execution and means nothing a week
# later.
#
# It came within one `git add -A` of a commit. The standing rule is to stage by
# path, and that rule held; but a rule is the only thing that was holding, and
# a rule is a person remembering. This is the instrument.
#
# NARROW ON PURPOSE — by extension, not by directory. scratchpad/ holds 38
# tracked files, DECISION-LOG.md among them, and that is the point of the
# folder: the reasoning lives there. Ignoring the directory would have quietly
# untracked the log the moment someone re-cloned.
scratchpad/**/*.png
scratchpad/**/*.jpg
scratchpad/**/*.jpeg
scratchpad/**/*.webp
scratchpad/**/*.gif
scratchpad/**/*.mp4
scratchpad/**/*.webm

# ── THE OWNER'S OWN FILES IN THE WORKING TREE ──────────────────────────────
#
# On 2026-09-15 `git add -A` staged the owner's untracked working folder into
# a feature commit. It was removed from the commit — and then DELETED FROM
# DISK by the next branch switch, because a staged path follows the index. It
# was recovered from a dangling commit via `git fsck --lost-found`.
#
# Ignoring these is the half that stops the sweep at the source: a path git
# will not stage is a path a checkout cannot carry away. .githooks/pre-commit
# is the other half, because .gitignore protection is only as old as the
# commit you stand on — scripts/check-no-credentials.mjs's own note, written
# after the same command committed a live credential DESPITE .gitignore.
#
# A file the owner put in the working tree is the owner's. The only permitted
# operations on it are none.
Claude outputs/
.claude/

# The declared-new-files list .githooks/pre-commit reads: a working note about
# one commit, never part of one.
.stage-paths
